      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering Key Management**\n\nI've decided to use Google Cloud KMS to handle key management. I'm focused on creating a `decrypt_payload.py` Python file. This file will be responsible for decrypting ciphertext payloads using the KMS service, so I need to make sure the key management is secure.\n\n\n**Defining Decryption Logic**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the specifics of the `decrypt_payload.py` file. I'm importing the `google-cloud-kms` library and planning a decryption function with the project ID, location, key ring, key name, and ciphertext as inputs. The plan is to use the KMS client for decryption, ensuring the provider is explicitly defined. I'm starting by creating the `decrypt_payload.py` file.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789867101042,
          "start": 1789867099737
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc648659001xcKC3pSO81T2iB",
